# Linux Fundamentals

  Started with basic navigation like ls and cd, then moved onto find -name passwords.txt for example, then also used the grep command to search for something within a file. example: grep "THM" access.log. 
  - ls: List the contents of the directory
  - cd: allows you to change directory
  - cat: Shows the contents of a file
  - pwd: print working directory, who am i?

  Then onto operators,
  - &: Runs the command but in the background, so allows you to keep working whilst it takes time to finish
  - &&: 2 commands to run but the second only after the first one has finished.
  - >: allows to redirect output into a file, will overwrite any current contents within that file
  - >>: This redirects the same as previous, but instead of overwritting it will add it onto the end of the file.

