  ## Processes101
        learnt about PID's and running processes,
          - Start: systemctl start myservice
          - Stop: systemctl stop myservice
          - Enable: systemctl enalbe myservice
          - Disable: systemctl disable myservice
          - Status: systemctl status myservice
        Using the T^Z or the & operator to run the services in the background, then using fg myservice to bring it back into the terminal.
        Different approaches to kill a process
          - SIGTERM - Kill the process, but allow it to do some cleanup tasks beforehand
          - SIGKILL - Kill the process - doesn't do any cleanup after the fact
          - SIGSTOP - Stop/suspend a process
